// compile-only: the plist output is asserted by TestGlobalVariableEncoding in cherri_test.go.
//
// Built-in globals (ShortcutInput, Clipboard, CurrentDate, Device, Ask) are identified by
// Type alone in native Shortcuts plists. A VariableName makes Shortcuts read them as a
// reference to a missing user-defined variable, so the global's value never reaches the
// action. Covers each place that encodes a variable reference: a Variable-typed action
// argument, a conditional's input value, and an inline interpolation.
//
// No #include needed here — the full test suite auto-injects every standard library category.

// Variable-typed action argument
setName(ShortcutInput, "Test")
wait(Ask)

// Conditional input value
if ShortcutInput {
    nothing()
}
if Clipboard {
    nothing()
}

// Inline interpolation
text("Clipboard was: {Clipboard}, date: {CurrentDate}, device: {Device}")

show("✅ All tests passed")
